# Reviewed gitleaks false positives, one fingerprint per line (commit:file:rule:line).
# Read by the "Secrets (gitleaks)" job in .github/workflows/security.yml via --gitleaks-ignore-path.
#
# A fingerprint names ONE finding in ONE commit. The same value committed again, in another
# file or on another line, is a new finding and fails again: that is the point. Never add a
# path-wide allowlist to gitleaks.toml instead.
#
# To add one: run the scan (BCWEB/guides/run/SECURITY_CI_EN.md, "Gitleaks"), read the finding
# in the redacted report, confirm the value is not a credential, and add its Fingerprint below
# with a comment saying WHY, the reviewer and the date. A real secret is never listed here: it
# is rotated first, and only then may its fingerprint be listed, with "rotated on <date>".
#
# Reviewed 2026-09-25 (agent-secci-bcw), every value read in the commit it was found in.
# NOT listed on purpose: BCWEB/infra/compose/.env.example:115 TELEMETRY_API_KEY in 63ecc8c6 and
# 9abfe0e3. The compose file calls it the public ingest key, but whether it is public by
# design (shipped inside the BMM client) was not verified; that is the owner's call, and until
# it is made the full-history run keeps reporting it.

